commit 1538873603a90367053d211b46c77eb61948aa45
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 23 16:53:02 2026 +0000

    The library's index parameters are bounded by Index, and a tuple of indices is an Index on both paths

    Unbounded, the subscript pair opr[i: I] beside opr[r: Range[\I\]] is invalid at I = Any: the range subscript is the more specific there, and its result is no element; the checker, reading symbolic operators, refused the pair at 124 sites of the library. Every index parameter of the generic indexed types is now I extends Index, ZZ32 extends Index and Range excludes it, and a tuple type whose element types are all Index types is a subtype of Index and outside Object, in the checker, in walk and in the specification, recorded in Appendix I as the revival's departure from the designers' tuple-type text (P-156); m[i, j] passes its tuple as before. Climb batch 21, rung B; its record folded into FACTS (F-278; F-245, F-81, F-259 brought up to date), the ledger (rows 805 and 806 added, 584 and 471 rewritten) and PLAN.md; the specification's sentences on Object and the hierarchy's root that the rule makes false corrected, with callouts.

